# Research reporting rules

- Cite the source for dataset, model and method facts.
- Record exact URLs and access dates.
- Never invent papers, authors, DOI values, quotations or citations.
- Clearly label prior-work claims, project design choices, hypotheses and measured findings.
- Do not claim novelty from component combination alone.
- Do not claim superiority unless a fair, repeated comparison supports it.
- State dataset limitations, licensing, domain, language and synthetic-data limitations.
- Explain negative, null and regressive results rather than hiding them.
- Every table and figure must be generated from saved experiment outputs or clearly marked as illustrative.
- Do not write conclusions before results exist.
- Use TODO placeholders in advance.
